# Needles on a wall (real TF2; ours: needles_wall.scene, fov_desired 75): a
# puppet Medic (stock Syringe Gun) on 2fort's bridge at 0 -300 0 facing
# the side wall (yaw 0, level: bot_teleport's pitch doesn't tilt a bot's
# aim), crouched so its aim meets the plank under the window, fires 0.3 s; watched in its eyes (`spec_mode 4`: FOV 75), pictures
# 0.5 s and 3 s after: the marks on the wood (specs/tf2/effects.md,
# "Needles on a wall").
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/needles_wall.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
cl_drawhud 0
r_drawvgui 0
r_drawviewmodel 0
tf_spec_xray 0
fov_desired 90
fps_max 60
mat_colorcorrection 0
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
sleep 1
jointeam spectator
sleep 2
bot_selectweaponslot 0
bot -name WallMedic -class medic -team red
sleep 3
bot_teleport WallMedic 0 -300 0 0 0 0
bot_selectweaponslot 0
sleep 2
spec_player WallMedic
sleep 1
spec_mode 4
sleep 1
bot_crouch 1
bot_teleport WallMedic 0 -300 0 0 0 0
sleep 3
shot wall_idle
bot_forceattack 1
sleep 0.3
bot_forceattack 0
sleep 0.5
shot wall_0_5
sleep 2.5
shot wall_3
bot_crouch 0
bot_kick all
